<title>ARGENTINA: SOCCER-ARGENTINA BEAT PERU 2-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-ARGENTINA BEAT PERU 2-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-06-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina beat Peru 2-0 (halftime 1-0) in a South American World Cup qualifier on Sunday.</p>
<p>Scorers: Hernan Crespo (45), Diego Simeone (47)</p>
<p>Attendance: 70,000</p>
<p>Standings (tabulate under played, won, drawn, lost, goals for, goals against, points)  Paraguay    10  7  2  1  15  6 23</p>
<p> Argentina   11  5  4  2  16 10 19</p>
<p> Colombia    11  5  3  3  16 10 18</p>
<p> Bolivia     10  3  5  2  15 10 14</p>
<p> Ecuador     11  4  2  5  15 13 14</p>
<p> Uruguay     11  4  2  5  11 15 14</p>
<p> Chile	 10  3  4  3  18 13 13</p>
<p> Peru	  11  3  4  4  11 14 13		</p>
<p> Venezuela   11  0  2  9   7 33  2</p>
<p>Next matches: July 6 - Paraguay v Argentina, Chile v Colombia, Peru v Bolivia, Venezuela v Ecuador</p>
<p>Note: top four teams qualify for the 1998 World Cup in France. Brazil qualify automatically as holders.</p>
</text>
